# Case A — AutoPlanner (CLC Workflow Automation)

## Client and problem
- **Client:** Supported Study Hall staff at the Center for Learning and Collaboration (CLC), Pomfret School.
- **Problem:** staff spend hours each week logging into individual student Canvas accounts and transcribing assignment data into to-do lists in Google Docs.
- **Goal:** keep one Google Doc per student, updated from Canvas automatically, that staff can reference without manual entry.

## Team
- Developers: Luke Ryan, Jack Weinberg. Club lead: Cayden Auyang. Staff contacts in the app and docs: Cayden Auyang and Luke Ryan.

## Stack and architecture (Google Apps Script only; there is no other server)
- `apps_script/` is the whole app, deployed as a web app on the Pomfret Google domain (`executeAs: USER_DEPLOYING`, `access: DOMAIN`, see `appsscript.json`).
  - `App.gs`: `doGet`, the `ALLOWED_USERS` check, student list and tokens in Script Properties (one property per student, `LockService` around writes), single and all-student updates in batches under the 6-minute limit with a `continueRun` trigger, daily triggers at 7 pm and midnight America/New_York, run summaries, `setupTriggers`, `checkSetup`, `scheduleTestRun`, `selfTest`.
  - `Canvas.gs`: Canvas REST client (UrlFetchApp, `fetchAll`, Link-header paging) plus week/day grouping. The output shape is what `Code.gs` reads.
  - `Code.gs`: writes each Doc with the Docs API: nested week tabs under "CLC Planner", stacked "By Class" and "By Day" tables, Status and Notes preserved across updates (keyed by Canvas assignment URL). It only updates Docs inside `DOCS_FOLDER_ID`.
  - `Index.html`: the staff page (HTML, CSS and JS in one file), talking to the server only through `google.script.run`.
- **Security rule:** `google.script.run` can call any function whose name doesn't end in `_`. Every internal function ends in `_`. Every public function starts with `requireAllowedUser_()` (page), `requireOwner_()` (editor-only) or `requireTrigger_(e)` (trigger handlers). `tests/app.test.js` lists the allowed public functions; update it deliberately.
- Tokens: never send them to the page (only the last 4 characters), never log them, never put them in an error message. Never store student data in a Sheet or Doc other than the planner Docs.
- **Deploying:** clasp is blocked for the owner's under-18 school account. Paste files with `scripts/copy-to-apps-script.sh`, then **Deploy → Manage deployments → Edit → New version**. Remind the developer that pasting alone doesn't change the live app.
- `frontend/index.html` is only the "AutoPlanner has moved" page on GitHub Pages.

## Constraints
- Keep the number of Apps Script files small (each one is a manual paste).
- Run `node --test tests/*.test.js` before every PR; add or update tests for any change in `apps_script/`. Tests use fake data only.
- Docs API quota: batch writes (see `BATCH_CHUNK` in `Code.gs`) and reuse the existing `documentId` rather than creating new Docs.
- Never commit secrets, tokens, real student data, staff email lists, or `.clasp.json` / `.clasprc.json`.

## Definition of done (current phase)
- Staff sign in with Pomfret accounts, add students, and every student's Doc updates automatically at about 7 pm and midnight; Status and Notes survive updates; `selfTest` passes in the live project.
